Falsifies `capability_plan::proofs::the_device_split_partitions_the_mappings`.

The defect: `PageKind::mode` returns `MAP_RW` for device registers as well as for shared
pages, so every device register window a component is endowed with is mapped writable.
A one-word slip in a short match, and the kind of thing a copy-paste produces.

Expected to fail: `assert!(m.2 == abi::address_space::MAP_RO)` over the late half of the
split, on any declaration containing a device page.

**Measured blind before milestone 211.** The harness used to assert
`m.2 == PageKind::DeviceRegisters.mode()`, and `plan` fills that word by calling
`kind.mode()`, so both sides moved together and this diff left the harness verifying.
Confirmed by applying it against the old phrasing and watching it stay green. The
constants are now written out, and the harness also asserts the two differ, so a defect
that collapsed them cannot pass by making the partition trivially uniform.

diff --git a/crates/capability_plan/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability_plan/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/capability_plan/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability_plan/src/lib.rs
@@ -277,7 +277,7 @@ impl PageKind {
     pub const fn mode(self) -> u64 {
         match self {
             PageKind::Shared => abi::address_space::MAP_RW,
-            PageKind::ReadOnly | PageKind::DeviceRegisters => abi::address_space::MAP_RO,
+            PageKind::ReadOnly | PageKind::DeviceRegisters => abi::address_space::MAP_RW,
         }
     }
 }
